Hi [~accountid:62ea2a6c96eb272011a8098d] 

Thanks for the ping and clarifying the urgency. To respond to the questions:

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* where can this be found on our website (exact paragraphs)?

Global Privacy Notice for Passengers (I assume BNP Paribas needs the German version) - [https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/de-de/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides|smart-link] 
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* what data is stored

This is clarified in Section 3 “What personal data do we process?”.

It clarifies that Bolt collects and processes personal data:

* provided by data subjects to Bolt;
* when data subjects use the Bolt App; and
* from other sources such as authorised third parties who administer services on behalf of Bolt (such as Bolt Business customers), and in some countries, governmental or public databases.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* where

This is clarified in:

 Sections 5 “Who do we share your personal data with?”

It clarifies the categories of recipients, including web hosting and cloud storage.

Section 6 “Does Bolt transfer your personal data to other countries?”

It clarifies how personal data may be transferred to, stored and/or processed by Bolt Group Companies, subcontractors and partners.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
* for how long?

This is clarified in Section 8 “How long do we retain your personal data for?”

It describes that Bolt keeps personal data only as long as necessary to provide our services and for the purposes described in the Section 4 “What purposes do we use your personal data for and what is our legal basis for processing?” of the Global Privacy Notice for Passengers.

This means that the retention periods will vary according to the type, the amount and sensitivity of the personal data, the potential risk of harm from unauthorised use or disclosure of the personal data and the reason that we have collected the personal data in the first place.
{panel}

