*Current status:*

The project began as an effort between privacy and procurement to renegotiate terms during the procurement review. First review completed in Q1 2024 - problematic agreements were identified & commented (no privacy terms, missing key privacy clauses).

Privacy and commerce agreed that in each case where we re-negotiate terms with our providers - privacy is looped in to support and re-negotiate / add privacy safeguards where necessary. Privacy contacted Commerce in August 2024 to follow up on the process and found a key issue: commerce providers are not included in the annual procurement review. It was excluded in September 2023.

Privacy aligned with commerce that privacy plans to reach out and re-negotiate with problematic providers in Q4 2024.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
*Next steps:*

# get back to the review in Q4, re-review the list, and prioritise re-negotiating depending on the issue.
# considering the recent case with Uber - providers with no SCCs / legacy SCCs will have to be prioritised. 
{panel}

