 I tried answering the questions but unfortunately, they are unclear and I can only provide a proper answer only for the first two. 

# *Why is Tesco a separate administrator?*

Both parties act as separate data controllers mainly because the purpose of personal data processing is different by Bolt and Partner (Tesco). To clarify:

* While Bolt processes user’s (client’s) personal data to offer information service to the Partner restaurant, Partner processes user’s personal data to fulfill sales agreement. 
* While Bolt offers ICT service to users and Partners, the Partner decides to use Bolt as service provider to connect with users, meaning that Partner decides on how the personal data is being processed which qualifies the Partner as a separate controller in providing its own service even if they use Bolt as service provider for aiding their service provision.

# *What personal data does Tesco receive from users?*

The personal data parties share (Tesco receives via Bolt platform) include: 

* First name and the first letter of the last name of the Client and the Delivery Partner;
* Phone number of the Client and the Delivery Partner;
* Order and the Order Price of the Client;
* Feedback left by the Client on the Bolt Food Platform in relation to the Partner (Tesco);
* Any other notes made by the Client in relation to the Order through the Bolt Food Platform.

Please, refer to Section 3.1. of the Schedule 2 of our Terms and Conditions for Partners available at: [https://bolt.eu/cs-cz/legal/tnc-bolt-food-partner/?category=delivery|https://bolt.eu/cs-cz/legal/tnc-bolt-food-partner/?category=delivery|smart-link] 

# *Who ensures the operation of the platform?*

{color:#bf2600}This seems as a question for the business. While Bolt ensures the technical functioning of the platform, the Partner also has some obligations, if I’m not mistaken. From the privacy perspective, what the Partner could mean is which Bolt entity operates the platform as what are the data flows (Estonia - CZ?). Can you please ask the Partner to clarify what they mean by this question?{color} 

# *What rules for the protection of personal data do customers follow?*

{color:#bf2600}Can you please ask the Partner to clarify who do they mean as “customers”? Couriers? Users? In general, can you ask to specify what information Tesco is interested in? {color}

As for parties to the agreement: both ensure that they comply with respective obligations contained in applicable data protection laws (Section 2.1. of the Schedule 2 of our Terms and Conditions for Partners).

# *How about direct marketing?*

{color:#bf2600}What about direct marketing? {color}😅{color:#bf2600}  Can you please ask them to clarify what do they mean? Does Tesco mean whether they can send direct marketing to users?{color}

Both parties ensure they have a valid legal basis for soliciting direct marketing to the client. Please refer to Section 5 of the Schedule 2 of our Terms and Conditions for Partners.

# *How about the satisfaction questionnaire and its validity?*

{color:#bf2600}Please, ask the Partner the same question as in regards to the previous one. {color}

# *or clarification of the entire processing setting.*

{color:#bf2600}Have we provided the Partner with the Schedule 2 of our Terms and Conditions for Partners (DSA)? Can you please ask the Partner to clarify what do they mean by this question? {color}

